  "scope": "Generic organic trunk closure and real bead-bearing repair, current uncommitted source, normal Release native tests and actual Release CLI. No commit, push or physical printing trial.",
  "causes": [
    "Organic sheath generation clipped its seam and inserted an inward open anchor.",
    "Continuation and pruning clipped boundary polylines into open hooks. Reclosing only an excised span could create a new airborne closing chord.",
    "Height modulation could discard direction-locked wall identity; ordinary infill bridge exemptions must not exempt trunk contours.",
    "Default square-join bead polygons overstated actual round-bead bearing at corners. Microscopic native closed loops could collapse at output precision yet count as full nominal support footprints."
  ],
  "repair": [
    "Generate complete oriented organic outer and inner contours at every branch size, preserving identity through height modulation.",
    "Clip filled cross-sections and extract closed contours. Restrict a replacement section to collision-free carried centers so its new closing chord is backed.",
    "Require complete local bearing of outer walls; retain legal two-ended straight bridges only for ordinary infill and interface.",
    "Use round actual bead envelopes and remove unprintable closed loops before contact and bearing capture and from newly generated repairs.",
    "Apply geometry and configured flow/slab/collision rules without printer-name or input-model-specific branches.",
    "Reuse exact footprint, eroded-footprint and allowed-center masks within the shared adaptive live-memory budget, invalidating mutable planes on every path change. Maximum requested budget is 256 MiB and 1/32 available RAM; low-memory or unknown readings use uncached scratch behavior."
  ],
