  "checker_semantics": "Explicit E0 XY steps no longer than 0.002 mm are retained inside extrusion circuits because five-decimal E quantization can round tiny moves to zero. Entire all-zero paths and stationary extrusion dots do not become full bead footprints. Native endpoints coincide exactly; exported endpoint differences are reported against the explicit coordinate-precision bound. Complete native walls are matched one-to-one to observed subcircuits, even after continuous infill prefixes.",
  "limits": [
    "Native walls are exactly closed. Their actual G-code circuits match within 0.05 mm Hausdorff displacement for fitting; measured endpoint differences are retained and bounded by sqrt(2)*0.001+0.0001 mm for XY quantization and subprecision segment removal. Full actual round-bead bearing is checked separately.",
    "Independent bearing uses actual emitted heights and round line-width envelopes, plus the nearest eligible printed model material at the configured bottom gap. Outer contours have no bridge exemption; only rounding-scale unbacked fragments are tolerated.",
    "Meaningful top-contact regions are retained, but unsupported fringes can be trimmed; exact contact area and old support paths are not preserved.",
    "The two provided cartesian projects and native variants are verified. This is geometric and regression evidence, not an all-model guarantee or a physical print-strength trial.",
    "Earlier local-bearing evidence did not prove closed contour topology. Intermediate v9 outputs retained real corner-bearing failures and sub-output-precision loops; they were not accepted."
  ],
